Additional Use Grant: You may make Production Use of the Licensed Work if,
at the time of that use, one of the following applies:

1. Personal Use. You are a natural person using the Licensed Work solely for
   personal, educational, research, or other non-commercial purposes.

2. Independent Professional Use. You are a natural person using the Licensed
   Work in your own capacity as an independent professional or sole trader,
   and your Professional Business is a Qualifying Small Organization. You may
   use the Licensed Work while providing services to a client of any size,
   provided the client does not install, operate, control, receive a copy of,
   or otherwise make its own Production Use of the Licensed Work under this
   grant.

3. Small Organization Use. You are making Production Use solely for the
   benefit of a Qualifying Small Organization.

A "Qualifying Small Organization" is an organization whose Controlled Group,
during its most recently completed fiscal year, had both:

* fewer than 25 People; and
* less than EUR 1,000,000 in Annual Revenue or annual operating budget.

"Organization" includes a company, partnership, sole proprietorship,
association, public body, non-profit organization, and any other legal or
economic undertaking.

"Professional Business" means the sole proprietorship or other undertaking
through which an independent professional provides services.

"People" means the average total number of employees and individual
independent contractors who worked for the Controlled Group during the fiscal
year, regardless of whether they were full-time or part-time.

"Annual Revenue" means worldwide gross revenue before costs, taxes, or other
deductions. Revenue or budgets denominated in another currency must be
converted to euros using the European Central Bank reference rate applicable
at the end of the fiscal year.

"Controlled Group" means the organization, every entity that controls it,
every entity it controls, and every entity under common control with it.
"Control" means direct or indirect ownership of more than 50 percent of the
voting interests or the power to direct management and policies by ownership,
contract, or otherwise.

If a person or organization ceases to qualify under paragraphs 2 or 3 solely
because it crosses a People, Annual Revenue, or operating-budget threshold,
its Production Use remains permitted for 90 days after the end of the fiscal
year in which the threshold was crossed. This transition period is solely to
obtain another license or stop Production Use.

This Additional Use Grant does not restrict any non-production rights already
granted by the Business Source License. For alternative licensing
arrangements, contact 686f6c61@00b.tech.

"Production Use" means use of the Licensed Work to perform or support ongoing
personal, professional, organizational, customer-facing, revenue-generating,
or operational work. It excludes evaluation, testing, development of the
Licensed Work itself, and demonstration in an environment that is not relied
on for actual work. If an organization or Professional Business has not
completed a fiscal year, eligibility is determined using a reasonable,
good-faith forecast of its People and Annual Revenue or operating budget for
the current fiscal year.

